.env
.DS_Store
grok-export/
__pycache__
ssrn-abstract-classifier
wandb
pwb_toolbox/datasets/logfile.log
*.egg-info
*.whl
*.tar.gz
.venv

server/airflow/airflow.db
server/airflow/logs/
server/airflow/simple_auth_manager_passwords.json.generated
trade_log.csv

# graphify - machine-specific sidecars (absolute paths / local cache)
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.vocab.txt

# graphify - regenerable output. GRAPH_REPORT.md (the written findings) and
# graph.json (the fixture tools/graph_audit.py reads) stay tracked; these two
# do not. graph.html is a 740 KB rendering of graph.json, and manifest.json is
# the incremental-rebuild index, keyed on float mtimes that differ on every
# machine — so it produced a large diff on every rebuild while meaning nothing.
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/manifest.json

# Strategy Lab run records: local test output, not source.
strategy-runs/
# desk agent: raw per-run stdout. Noise, and it can contain chart detail.
# runs.jsonl (the structured record) and out/ (gameplans, Pine reports) stay
# tracked -- they are the agent's memory and its deliverables.
tools/desk_agent/logs/

# per-business engagement data (tools/engagement.py) — this fork is public,
# and a client's process map and findings are confidential. Only the README
# explaining that is tracked.
engagements/*
!engagements/README.md

# speculative paper-trading ledger (tools/spec_desk.py) — personal trade
# records, and this fork is public. Only the README explaining that is tracked.
spec_desk/*
!spec_desk/README.md

# overnight stress lab (tools/night_lab.py) - derived from personal trade
# records, and this fork is public. Only the README explaining that is tracked.
night_lab/*
!night_lab/README.md

# seasonality lab (tools/season_scan.py) - universe.txt names what the
# owner watches and the report derives from it; this fork is public.
season/*
!season/README.md
# Pine converter corpus (docs/converter-corpus.md) - fetched scripts and their
# manifest. Regenerable by re-running the fetch, and large; not source.
corpus/

# market_close render output - per-segment TTS script text, regenerated every
# run and derived from the day's tape.
render/

# planner_watch local run state. Machine-specific, and the .bak is a scratch
# copy of the example rather than the tracked example itself.
watch-state.json
watch-state.example.bak

# Obsidian vault mirror (tools/obsidian_sync.py) - this fork is public and the
# vault is the Claude config repo, whose Projects/ tree holds session
# transcripts with personal detail. Decided 2026-08-29: the vault is not
# mirrored into this repository at all. Ignored rather than merely guarded, so
# an accidental sync followed by `git add -A` cannot publish it.
docs/journal/
dist/

# `npx skills` staging copy. The installed skill is committed under
# .claude/skills/; this mirror is restorable with `npx skills experimental_install`.
.agents/
